// every 5 s; faster with the cable in). Two faults:
//  1. A web request handled on the other core (sign, NIP-44, /api/sig...) ends
//     with pwrIdle(), which took the WHOLE chip to 80 MHz in the middle of a
//     scan: the documented "~1 fps, looks frozen" pattern. While a scan holds
//     the camera, pwrIdle() now leaves the clock alone.
